<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<!--
	Appearance of the raid boss book, opened by right clicking the book item.

	Everything the player sees is defined here - every single string included, so no player facing
	text is left in the Java. The behavior (whether the book exists at all, how many kills a hunting
	level takes, what a new level rewards, how many points a kill is worth and how much damage a
	hunting level adds) lives server side, on config/mods/raidbook.properties.

	Which item opens the book isn't set anywhere here either : the book is bound to an item by the
	"handler" attribute of data/xml/items ("RaidBossBook"), so any amount of items can carry it.

	The book holds three pages.

	The main list opens on a head telling the very player where he stands on the server wide ladder,
	along with a link to it, then the level filter menu, then one row per raid boss :

		Место: 12             1 250 очк.     Рейтинг
		============================================
		Все    1-20   20-40   40-60   60-80
		Greyclaw Kutus  Ур.23           ур.3   Инфо
		[############........] 12/15

	A row draws the name and the level of the boss on one line and the progress bar of the hunting
	level right under it - the way the experience bar of a character reads - followed by the kills
	done over the kills the next level takes.

	The bar is built out of table cells, one per half, and not out of two images written next to each
	other : the client breaks the line right after an image, so two of them inside one single cell
	land on two lines and the bar shows up cut in half. That is also why a row is two stacked tables
	sharing one background color rather than one table - a bar can't share a table with text sitting
	in columns of its own.

	A detail page opens on the statistics of the boss, laid out the way the status window of a
	character is - two blocks of two columns - then the hunting block, the buttons, and the four tabs :

		HP  ...   Exp ...          the pools on the left column, the rewards on the right one
		MP  ...   SP  ...
		========================   the hairline cutting the blocks apart
		Физ.Атака  ...  Маг.Атака  ...
		Физ.Защита ...  Маг.Защита ...
		Скор.Атаки ...  Скор.Каста ...
		========================
		Ур.охоты  3     Убийств    12
		Бонус урона 3%  До уровня   3
		     [############........] 12/15
		========================
		Назад                 Искать
		Награды  Дроп  История  Рейтинг

	Every number of the statistics block is computed out of the template of the boss rather than out
	of a live instance : a boss which is dead, or simply not spawned yet, has to be readable too. The
	defences carry "RaidDefenceMultiplier" of config/npcs/bosses.properties, and the experience and
	the SP are what the very player reading the book would earn for a solo kill - server rates and
	level gap penalty folded in.

	"Искать" drops a radar marker on the spawn point of the boss, which is what the arrow circling the
	character then points at. A boss standing in the world is marked where it actually stands.

	The ladder page is the same list, holding the position, the name, the clan and the score of each
	player, the row of the reader being written with the "self" color. Its head links to the daily
	reward page, which tells what each rewarded position of the ladder is handed every day.

	The item icons come from data/xml/itemIcons.xml.

	<layout>
		Sizes of the generated tables. Every table of a page is generated out of the very same
		width, which is what keeps them aligned - never describe one on the HTM.

		width       : width, in pixels, of every generated table. Fed to the HTMs as %width%. Keep
		              it below 290, so the scrollbar doesn't eat the last column.
		rowHeight   : total height, in pixels, of a row of the main list. Such a row is two stacked
		              lines - the name and the progress bar - and this is both of them together : the
		              name line takes "groupHeight", the bar line whatever is left. So keep it above
		              groupHeight, and roughly twice it.
		groupHeight : height, in pixels, of the one line rows : the filter menu, the tab menu, the
		              button row, the page selector and every row of a detail page tab.
		headerHeight     : height, in pixels, of a single line of a two columns block - the
		                   statistics of a boss and the hunting block.
		headerLabelWidth : width, in pixels, of one caption cell of those blocks. A block is two
		                   columns wide, so the value of a column takes what is left of that column -
		                   ((width - headerGap) / 2) - headerLabelWidth - and the numbers are written
		                   with their thousand separators, so leave it room. A caption which doesn't
		                   fit wraps, and a wrapped line is taller than "headerHeight", which throws
		                   the bottom padding of the page off.
		headerGap        : width, in pixels, of the spacer sitting between the two columns. Without
		                   it the caption of the right column would touch the value of the left one,
		                   which is right aligned on the column edge. 0 drops it.
		iconSize    : size, in pixels, the item icons are drawn at.
		pageWidth   : width, in pixels, of a single cell of the page selector - a page link or an
		              arrow. It is what keeps the selector on a single line : the amount of shown
		              links is whatever fits "width" out of that. Raise it if a selector ever wraps.
		maxPages    : maximum amount of page links shown by the page selector, centered on the
		              current page. It only ever lowers the amount "pageWidth" already allows.
		nameChars   : amount of characters above which an item or character name is shortened, on the
		              last word boundary when possible. 0 never shortens - and lets a long name wrap,
		              which makes its row taller than the others. Those names own their column whole,
		              so this is roughly the column width divided by 6.
		bossNameChars : the same, for the name of a raid boss on the main list. It gets a limit of
		              its own, and a tighter one, because it shares its line with the level of that
		              boss ("Greyclaw Kutus Ур.23") - the level has to fit next to it, whatever the
		              name. Roughly (listNameWidth / 6) minus the length of "levelPrefix" and of the
		              level itself.
		ellipsis    : suffix appended to a shortened name.
		separator   : client texture of the hairline cutting a page into blocks. It is always drawn
		              1 pixel tall - the height a page is padded up to counts on that. An empty
		              value drops every rule.
		overhead    : height, in pixels, everything but the rows takes on the HTM - the hairline
		              above the page selector and the closing spacer. Substracted from pageHeight to
		              know how much the page has to be padded with. Only worth touching after
		              editing the HTMs. Rough guide : <br> 16, <br1> 8, a separator img 1, a
		              selector row 18. The stock HTMs add up to 27.
		pageHeight  : total height, in pixels, every page is padded up to. Since it is the very same
		              on every page, the page selector always lands on the same spot ; and since it
		              is set slightly above the height of the dialog, the scrollbar stays shown
		              everywhere. 0 disables the padding.

		screenTime  : how long, in milliseconds, an informational message stays on the screen of the
		              player it is sent to. The chat always gets those messages ; whether the screen
		              gets them too is "RaidBookScreenMessages" of the properties.

		barWidth / barHeight : size, in pixels, of the progress bar of a hunting level. The bar owns
		                       a line of its own and starts on the left edge, so barWidth only has to
		                       leave room for the counter written right after it - the counter cell
		                       takes (width - barWidth).
		barFilled / barEmpty : client textures the filled and the empty parts of that bar are drawn
		                       with. They are the one place the bar gets its look from : swapping
		                       them for the gauge textures of a rebuilt client is all it takes to
		                       make it read exactly like the experience bar. An empty value leaves
		                       that half of the bar blank without moving anything - the cell keeps
		                       its width - so emptying "barEmpty" alone shows the filled part only.

		The five sets of column widths below must each sum up to the layout width, otherwise the
		rows of that table won't be aligned - a mismatch is warned about in the log.

		listNameWidth / listLevelWidth / listButtonWidth       : rows of the main list - the name and
		                                                         the bar, the hunting level and the
		                                                         counter of the bar, the link to the
		                                                         detail page.
		dropIconWidth / dropNameWidth / dropChanceWidth        : rows of the "drop" tab. The group
		                                                         headers are cut out of the same
		                                                         widths - caption on the left, group
		                                                         chance on the "dropChanceWidth".
		rewardIconWidth / rewardNameWidth / rewardLevelWidth   : rows of the "rewards" tab, and of
		                                                         the daily reward page.
		historyNameWidth / historyClanWidth / historyTimeWidth : rows of the "history" tab.
		rankPosWidth / rankNameWidth / rankClanWidth
		    / rankPointsWidth                                  : rows of the ladders.

	<colors>
		Every color of the book. An empty value keeps the client default : a transparent background
		for a row, a plain white text for a label.

		row / altRow      : background of the odd / even bands of a page.
		name              : names of the raid bosses, of the items and of the ranked players.
		groupText         : caption of a drop group header.
		bossLevel         : level of a raid boss, written next to its name.
		huntLevel         : hunting level of the reader, and the level a reward belongs to.
		label / value     : captions and values of the two columns blocks.
		count             : amounts - the dropped ones, the reward ones and the ranking points.
		tab / activeTab   : tab links and buttons / the shown tab and the "Искать" button.
		filter / activeFilter : filter links / the shown level range.
		page / activePage : page links / the current page.
		self              : the row of the very player reading a ladder.
		disabled          : the label shown instead of an empty list.

		highChance / mediumChance / lowChance : chances of the "drop" tab, split by the two
		                                        thresholds below.
		highChanceFrom / mediumChanceFrom     : those thresholds, in percent.

	<labels>
		bookTitle / rankTitle / dailyTitle : title bars of the main list, of the ladder page and of
		                        the daily reward page. A detail page titles itself with the name and
		                        the level of its boss.
		daily                 : caption of the link leading from the ladder to the daily rewards.
		placeSuffix           : appended to a ranking position on that page, "1" reading as "1 место".
		                        The leading space belongs to the attribute.
		dropGroup             : caption of a drop group header, followed by the rank of the group -
		                        a boss reads "Дроп #1, Дроп #2". Every group of a raid boss carries
		                        it, since a raid boss isn't spoiled.
		numberPrefix          : sits between that caption and the rank of the group.

		The captions below name the columns of the lists which need it - the ladders, the history and
		the daily reward page. They are drawn once on top of their list rather than sliced along with
		its rows, so they stay readable whatever page is browsed, and they take the "groupText" color.
		The reward and the drop tabs have none : a reward list reads itself, and a drop group header
		already says what sits under it.

		colPos / colName / colClan   : columns of the ladders - position, character, clan.
		colPoints                    : score column of the server wide ladder, which counts points.
		colKills                     : score column of a per boss ladder, which counts kills.
		colName / colClan / colTime  : columns of the history - killer, his clan, when it happened.
		colReward / colPlace         : columns of the daily reward page. A position handing out
		                               several items lists them one per row, and only the first of
		                               them carries the position.
		levelPrefix           : put in front of the level of a raid boss, and of the level a reward
		                        belongs to.
		huntLevelPrefix       : put in front of the hunting level on a row of the main list. It sits
		                        in a "listLevelWidth" wide cell, so keep it short.
		details / search / back / rank : the four links - the detail page of a boss, the radar
		                                 marker, the way back to the list, the ladder.
		rankPrefix            : put in front of the position of the reader on the head of a page.
		unranked              : shown instead of that position, to whoever holds no point at all.
		points                : appended to the amount of ranking points on the head of a page - a
		                        bare number wouldn't tell what it counts. The leading space belongs
		                        to the attribute.
		hunt / kills / bonus / nextLevel : captions of the hunting block - the hunting level, the
		                                   amount of kills, the damage bonus that level grants and
		                                   the amount of kills the next one still takes.
		maxLevel              : shown instead of the kills left, when "RaidBookMaxLevel" is set and
		                        the cap has been reached.
		tabRewards / tabDrop / tabHistory / tabRank : captions of the four tabs of a detail page.
		hp / mp / exp / sp    : captions of the first statistics block - the HP and the MP pools of
		                        the boss on the left column, the experience and the SP the kill is
		                        worth to the player reading the book on the right one.
		pAtk / pDef / atkSpd  : captions of the left column of the second block.
		mAtk / mDef / castSpd : captions of its right column.
		noClan                : shown instead of the clan of a killer who had none.
		empty                 : shown instead of an empty list.
		notFound              : sent to whoever asks for a raid boss which doesn't exist any more.
		noLocation            : sent to whoever asks to be pointed at a boss which owns no spawn
		                        point at all.
		searchDone            : sent along the radar marker.

		The four messages below are what the book tells a player about his own hunting. They all go
		to the chat ; the last three also go to the screen when "RaidBookScreenMessages" allows it -
		the kill one doesn't, it would flash on every single kill. Emptying one silences it.

		msgKill               : sent on a raid boss kill, to everyone credited for it. Holds the
		                        %boss% and %points% variables.
		msgLevelUp            : sent when a hunting level is reached. Holds %boss% and %level%.
		msgReward             : sent along each item a hunting level rewards. Holds %level%, %item%
		                        and %count%.
		msgDaily              : sent along each item a daily ladder reward gives - on the spot when
		                        the winner is online, on his next login otherwise. Holds %place%,
		                        %item% and %count%.
		countPrefix           : put in front of an amount, which tells it apart from the item name
		                        sitting next to it.
		countRange            : sits between the two bounds of a dropped amount which isn't fixed.
		chancePattern         : DecimalFormat pattern a chance is rendered with, its amount of
		                        decimals included. It is used by the damage bonus too.
		chanceSuffix          : appended to a rendered chance.
		nearZero              : shown instead of a chance the pattern would round down to a bare
		                        zero, which would read as "never". Holds its own suffix, and is
		                        worth rewriting along with "chancePattern".
		timePattern           : SimpleDateFormat pattern a kill date of the history is written with.
		prevPage / nextPage   : labels of the page selector arrows. Both live in a "pageWidth" wide
		                        cell, so keep them short.

		A label needing a "&lt;" or a "&gt;" writes it as an XML entity, the way "nearZero" and the
		page arrows do. The book escapes them back on its way to the client, so a bare angle bracket
		would be swallowed as the start of a tag and take the rest of its cell with it.

	<filters>
		The level filter menu sitting on the head of the main list, one cell per entry, in the very
		order they are written here. They are cut out of the layout width, so adding entries makes
		every cell narrower - keep the labels short.

		label     : what the cell reads.
		min / max : the level range, both bounds included. A range of 0 to 0 matches every raid boss,
		            which is what the "Все" entry is.
-->
<list>
	<layout width="280" rowHeight="36" groupHeight="18" headerHeight="16" headerLabelWidth="76" headerGap="6" iconSize="32" pageWidth="26" maxPages="10" nameChars="24" bossNameChars="17" ellipsis="..." separator="L2UI.SquareGray" overhead="27" pageHeight="440" screenTime="5000" barWidth="120" barHeight="7" barFilled="L2UI.SquareWhite" barEmpty="L2UI.SquareGray" listNameWidth="160" listLevelWidth="54" listButtonWidth="66" dropIconWidth="36" dropNameWidth="190" dropChanceWidth="54" rewardIconWidth="36" rewardNameWidth="190" rewardLevelWidth="54" historyNameWidth="108" historyClanWidth="92" historyTimeWidth="80" rankPosWidth="30" rankNameWidth="104" rankClanWidth="78" rankPointsWidth="68" />

	<colors row="000000" altRow="" name="" groupText="LEVEL" bossLevel="B09878" huntLevel="LEVEL" label="B09878" value="FFFFFF" count="B09878" tab="" activeTab="LEVEL" filter="" activeFilter="LEVEL" page="" activePage="LEVEL" self="LEVEL" disabled="707070" highChance="90EE90" mediumChance="BDB76B" lowChance="F08080" highChanceFrom="80" mediumChanceFrom="5" />

	<labels bookTitle="Книга рейдбоссов" rankTitle="Рейтинг охотников" dailyTitle="Ежедневные награды" daily="Награды дня" placeSuffix=" место" levelPrefix="Ур." huntLevelPrefix="ур." details="Инфо" search="Искать" back="Назад" rank="Рейтинг" rankPrefix="Место: " unranked="-" points=" очк." hunt="Ур.охоты" kills="Убийств" bonus="Бонус урона" nextLevel="До уровня" maxLevel="макс." tabRewards="Награды" tabDrop="Дроп" tabHistory="История" tabRank="Рейтинг" dropGroup="Дроп" numberPrefix=" #" colPos="#" colName="Имя" colClan="Клан" colPoints="Очки" colKills="Убийств" colTime="Когда" colReward="Награда" colPlace="Место" hp="HP" mp="MP" exp="Exp" sp="SP" pAtk="Физ.Атака" pDef="Физ.Защита" atkSpd="Скор.Атаки" mAtk="Маг.Атака" mDef="Маг.Защита" castSpd="Скор.Каста" noClan="-" empty="Здесь пусто" notFound="Такого рейдбосса нет." noLocation="Местоположение этого рейдбосса неизвестно." searchDone="Местоположение отмечено на карте." msgKill="%boss%: +%points% очков рейтинга." msgLevelUp="Уровень охоты на %boss% повышен до %level%!" msgReward="Награда за %level% ур. охоты: %item% x%count%." msgDaily="Ежедневная награда за %place% место: %item% x%count%." countPrefix="x" countRange="-" chancePattern="#0.##" chanceSuffix="%" nearZero="&lt;0.01%" timePattern="dd.MM HH:mm" prevPage="&lt;&lt;" nextPage="&gt;&gt;" />

	<filters>
		<filter label="Все" min="0" max="0" />
		<filter label="1-20" min="1" max="20" />
		<filter label="20-40" min="21" max="40" />
		<filter label="40-60" min="41" max="60" />
		<filter label="60-80" min="61" max="80" />
	</filters>
</list>
